    "text": "# _1. Preliminary definitions_ \n\nLet _S ⊂_ R<sup>_nλ_</sup> be a _nλ_ -simplex with vertexes [ **_λ_** 0 _, . . . ,_ **_λ_** _n_ ]. Let _L_ , with 0 _< L < ∞_ , be the Lipschitz constant of _θ_<sup>ˆ</sup> over Ω **_λ_** such that \n\n\n\nLet the diameter of a _nλ_ -simplex _S_ be the maximum distance between any two points belonging to the simplex, which is the maximum distance between two vertexes \n\n\n\nand let **_λ_** _i∗_ and **_λ_** _j∗_ be the most distant vertices such that _σ_ ( _S_ ) = �� **_λ_** _i∗ −_ **_λ_** _j∗_ ��. For each branching step _k_ = 1 _, . . . , K_ , let _Lk_ be the list of disjoint simplexes covering the feasible domain, that is<sup>�</sup> _j_<sup>_S_</sup> _k_<sup>(</sup><sup>_j_)</sup> = Ω for _Sk_<sup>(</sup><sup>_j_)</sup> _∈Lk_ and _Sk_<sup>(</sup><sup>_i_)</sup> � _Sk_ ( _j_ ) = ∅ _∀Sk_<sup>(</sup><sup>_i_)</sup><sup>_, S_</sup> _k_<sup>(</sup><sup>_j_)</sup> _∈Lk_ . Finally, let _lb_ : _S → R_ be a function bounding _θ_<sup>ˆ</sup> from below in the simplex _S_ \n\n\n\nand denote _lb_ ( _S_ ) its minimum \n\n\n\nThus, _lb_ ( _S_ ) is the lower bound for the minimum of _θ_<sup>ˆ</sup> in the simplex. Similarly, denote _ub_ ( _S_ ) the upper bound for the minimum of _θ_<sup>ˆ</sup> in the simplex. \n\n# _2. Bounding_ \n\nBecause _θ_<sup>ˆ</sup> is Lipschitz continuous, the lower bounding function _lb_ : _S →_ R can be defined as \n\n\n\nwhere **_λ_** _j_ are the vertexes of the simplex. The lower bound value _lb_ ( _S_ ) is therefore the minimum of _lb_ ( **_λ_** ) over the simplex _S_ \n\n\n\nFor the upper bound of the minimum, the minimum of the fitness values at the simplex vertexes is chosen as trivial bound \n\n\n\n17 \n\n"
